A public company must have basic legal documents.\par
\u9658?\cf3 One\cf2\par
\u9658?Two\par
\u9658?Three\par
\u9658?Five\par
\~\par
\ul\b Question No: 5\~\~\~\~\~ (Marks: 1) - Please choose one\ulnone\b0\par
According to section 305(b) of Company Ordinance 1984, a company may be wound up\par
by the court if number of members fall below in case of public company.\par
\u9658?Two\par
\u9658?Five\par
\u9658?Eight\par
\u9658?\cf3 Seven\par
\cf2\~\par
\ul\b Question No: 6\~\~\~\~\~ (Marks: 1) - Please choose one\ulnone\b0\par
If a very successful fast food restaurant has been ignoring customers' concerns about the small war toys and toy guns included in their Kids Meals, then managers should begin focusing on improving the firm's:\par
\u9658?\cf3 Ethics\par
\cf2\u9658?Profitability.\par
\u9658?Productivity.\par
\u9658?Game plan\par
\~\par
\ul\b Question No: 7\~\~\~\~\~ (Marks: 1) - Please choose one\ulnone\b0\par
\'85\'85\'85\'85\'85is a dimension of social responsibility that includes hiring minority\par
workers, making safe products, minimizing pollution, using energy wisely, and providing a safe work environment\par
\u9658?Corporate philanthropy\par
\u9658?Corporate policy\par
\u9658?Corporate governance\par
\u9658?\cf3 Corporate responsibility\cf2\par
\~\par
\ul\b Question No: 8\~\~\~\~\~ (Marks: 1) - Please choose one\ulnone\b0\par
At WAH Industries, new workers are immediately assigned to jobs. They learn by doing the actual work and by watching longer-term employees. WAH uses a policy of:\par
\~\par
\u9658?Vertical assimilation.\par
\u9658?\cf3 On-the-job training.\cf2\par
\u9658?Job rotation.\par
\u9658?Vestibule training\par
\~\par
\ul\b Question No: 9\~\~\~\~\~ (Marks: 1) - Please choose one\ulnone\b0\par
\'85\'85..was the management theorist who developed a model of the order in\par
which people strive to satisfy their needs:\par
\u9658?Frederick Strauss\par
\u9658?Frederick Taylor\par
\u9658?\cf3 Abraham Maslow\cf2\par
\u9658?Abraham Mayo\par
\~\par
\ul\b Question No: 10\~\~\~\~\~ (Marks: 1) - Please choose one\ulnone\b0\par
ABC Company is currently hiring employees from different countries. ABC Company is\par
said to be implementing strategy.\par
\u9658?\cf3 Decentralization\cf2\par
\u9658?Downsizing\par
\u9658?Workforce diversity\par
\u9658?Retrenchment\par
\~\par
\ul\b Question No: 11\~\~\~\~\~ (Marks: 1) - Please choose one\ulnone\b0\par
Specifications of a product relate to the:\par
\u9658?Physical characteristics and level of quality\par
\u9658?Types of service that are provided along with the product Financing available with the product\par
\u9658? Types of competitors offering a similar product\par
\~\par
\ul\b Question No: 12\~\~\~\~\~ (Marks; 1) - Please choose one\ulnone\b0\par
\'85\'85\'85occurs when there is direct communication between a seller and an\par
individual customer using a promotion method other than face-to-face personal selling.\par
\u9658? Direct marketing\par
\u9658? Personal marketing\par
\u9658? Direct distribution\par
\u9658? Interpersonal promotion\par
\~\par
\ul\b Question No: 13\~\~\~\~\~ (Marks; 1) - Please choose one\ulnone\b0\par
Which of the following parts are included in the marketing mix?\par
\u9658? \cf3 Product, place, promotion, and price\cf2\par
\u9658? Competition and customer satisfaction\par
\u9658? Buying, selling, transporting and storing\par
\u9658? Profit, distribution, and advertising\par
\~\par
\ul\b Question No: 14\~\~\~\~\~ (Marks: 1) - Please choose one\ulnone\b0\par
A cohesive marketing mix consists of the product, promotion, price, and\par
\u9658? Personnel\par
\u9658? Production\par
\u9658? Communication\par
\u9658?\cf3 Place\par
\cf2\~\par
\ul\b Question No: 15\~\~\~\~\~ (Marks; 1) - Please choose one\ulnone\b0\par
Marketers use market segmentation to:\par
\u9658? To link market needs to an organization's marketing program\par
\u9658? To relate supply to demand in economic terms.\par
\u9658? To develop specific marketing actions related to the 4 P's.\par
\u9658? \cf3 All of the given options\par
\~\par
\cf2\ul\b Question No: 16\~\~\~\~\~ (Marks; 1) - Please choose one\ulnone\b0\par
In the marketing research process the 1st step is to define the problem followed by:\par
\u9658? Implementing plan\par
\u9658? Collection of data\par
\u9658? Developing recommendation\par
\u9658? \cf3 Developing the research design\par
\cf2\~\par
\ul\b Question No: 17\~\~\~\~\~ (Marks: 1) - Please choose one\ulnone\b0\par
The marketing objective for the maturity stage of the Product life cycle is to:\par
\u9658? \cf3 Maintain brand loyalty\par
\cf2\u9658? Stress differentiation\par
\u9658? Harvest\par
\u9658?\~Gain awareness\par
When a company retains the product but reduces marketing support costs, it is in what stage of the Product life cycle?\par
\u9658? \cf3 Decline\par
\cf2\u9658? Maturity\par
\u9658? Growth\par
\u9658? Introduction\par
\~\par
\ul\b Question No: 19\~\~\~\~\~ (Marks; 1) - Please choose one\ulnone\b0\par
The value of a brand which is in some instances listed on a firm's balance sheet is known as:\par
\u9658? Brand equity\par
\u9658? Brand values\par
\u9658? Brand property\par
\u9658? Brand promise\par
\~\par
\ul\b Question No: 20\~\~\~\~\~ (Marks; 1) - Please choose one\ulnone\b0\par
Setting the highest initial price is called price:\par
\u9658? Penetration\par
\u9658? Gouging\par
\u9658? Parity\par
\u9658? Skimming\par
